 ## Subtopics
 
 ### Tetrahedralization-based Mesh Extraction
-A variant that decouples mesh resolution from Gaussian distribution, enabling fine meshing of restricted scene segments. It performs tetrahedralization of vertices, classifies tets as inside/outside based on sampled interior points, and extracts separating faces. It prioritizes smoothness and artifact reduction over raw metric gains, producing topologically clean surfaces for complex scenes like those in MipNeRF 360 [S22].
